Sentinel — Comprehensive Security System Fix & Redesign

You are working on Sentinel, a specialist Discord server security bot built using the existing MomentumOne framework and Python implementation.

Your task is to audit, fix, improve, and test the existing security system end to end. Do not simply hide warnings, change displayed permission values, or redesign the dashboard while leaving the underlying logic broken.

The primary goals are:

1. Fix incorrect permission and role-hierarchy checks.
2. Repair the setup, security, lockdown, and explain commands.
3. Build a complete, interactive Security Dashboard.
4. Activate all three security modes, including automatic observability and hybrid operation.
5. Make every security feature understandable and configurable.
6. Preserve the existing architecture and avoid regressions.

Inspect the entire relevant codebase before making changes.

